this is lucy james speaking for  alessandra for larry  now in this guide i'm gonna break down  seven essential tips for getting started  in mortal shell  and i'm gonna do it without mentioning  dark souls once  except for that mention right there the  swampy forest of fulgrim  serves as your hub which connects to the  three core dungeons in mortal shell  and it can be surprisingly easy to get  lost in its labyrinthine structure  early on in the game you'll arrive at  the fulgrim tower in addition to being  the place to swap shells and weapons  it also houses many of mortal shells  npcs  including a merchant sesta ganesa who  can upgrade your shells  and a workbench to improve your weapons  secrets items and dungeons are all  accessible the more you explore fulgrim  and be sure to explore these smaller  tunnels as they can help you skip  different areas and make your journey  from point a to point b  easier also keep an eye out for large  stone tablets  which you can read for lore and which  hold clues about hidden spots  while you'll face many monsters  throughout the game there are still  several friendly faces to find in  fulgrim who will have your back  the most important ally you have in your  adventure is sister ganesa  not only will she upgrade your shells  but she will also fill you in on some  crucial details  about the game's world to help offer  context and perspective  even giving you clues on where to go  next if you max out a particular shell's  upgrades  she'll instead sell you useful  consumables  there's also an easily missed vendor at  the top of the tower near its bell  who will sell weapon upgrades and a  special kit that gets you one of the  only ranged weapons in the game  don't miss them at the beginning of  mortal shell you'll familiarize yourself  with the protagonist  known as the foundling the foundling  isn't too resilient in a fight which  means they'll die  in only one hit to overcome this the  foundling can possess the bodies of long  deceased  warriors who have met their end in the  land of falgrim  allowing them to adopt their combat  skills and resilience  the first shell you'll find in the game  is harros a well-rounded warrior who has  fairly even health and stamina bars  eventually you'll find three other  shells that possess the familiar rpg  archetypes that focus on speed  resolve and defensive attributes even  before venturing into  the first dungeon you can find all four  characters  giving you options on how to proceed  with the rest of the game  some of these shells have advantages  over others so if you have a favorite  you're free to stick with them  throughout the game  still it's essential to learn what their  limits are and prioritize which skills  you should unlock  first in their skill menu if you feel  you want to switch over to a different  shell fast then be sure to keep an eye  out for items known as  effigies which can be used to switch  over to different characters while out  in the field  as you take on more foes and survive in  combat you'll begin to build up charges  of resolve  your pool of resolve which is located  just above your health meter  can be spent to engage special skills  and abilities in combat  in addition to a useful kick attack  which can be unlocked in your shell's  skill menu  you can also activate buffs for your  weapons you can also unlock specialized  weapon skills when upgrading your gear  letting you take down stronger prey or a  smaller group of enemies with ease  while you may feel inclined to use your  resolve when you've got it it's much  better to save them for when you need  them most  for instance the most useful repast  mechanic comes in clutch when you need  to restore health  but it costs a single bar of resolve to  use so be sure to keep track of your  resolve  while out in the field the most  invaluable skill that you'll need to  master is the ability to harden  this skill allows the foundling to  instantly turn to stone  making them and their shell invulnerable  to nearly every attack in the game  aside from certain grabs from the more  elite monsters  you can activate harden at any time even  mid attack  and this ability can be especially  useful when fighting some of the  aggressive and  quick enemies it's an incredibly useful  skill and when you learn the enemy's  attack patterns  you can actively use this knowledge  against them to set up some deadly  strikes  to win the fight  another incredibly useful defensive  skill is the parry  after making it to the fulgrim tower at  the beginning of the game you'll find a  large character called the old prisoner  shackled on the second floor  examining the item on the staircase next  to it will grant you the tarnished seal  once acquired you'll be able to use  parries in combat which can knock  enemies off balance  the tarnished seal opens up two  different forms of parrying the perfect  parry and the riposte  if you don't have any resolve you can  only use the perfect parry  this version requires some more precise  timing to nail but it will not only  knock  foes off balance after their standard  attack it will also restore  a single resolved charge if you have a  resolved charge then you can use the  riposte  this version of the parry will not only  stagger enemies but also opens them up  for a special attack  that restores some of your health  throughout your exploration of falgrim  you'll acquire a variety of items from  the ground  and from hidden chests but as you  examine these items you'll see that  you'll need to use them to learn of  their effects  each item has a familiarity level and  when you keep using that item  your character will gain knowledge about  it when you manage to max out  familiarity with one item after repeated  uses  you'll unlock its true potential you'll  also find that certain items like  healing mushrooms will respawn after a  certain time  so you'll rarely be out of some items  for long  maxing out familiarity can be great for  healing items and other objects that  offer buffs to your character  however some items present an initial  risk  for example the taskbar mushroom deals  poison damage to you when you first  use it once you max out familiarity with  the force it grants you temporary  immunity  to poison damage we'll have plenty more  to share on mortal shells so check out  our channel for our official review  as well as some neat guides on how to  unlock the game's hard mode  if you've got any more mortal shell tips  to share make sure to put them in the  comments below  thanks for watching and we'll see you  next time  you
 

